WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
They also, my parents also, were one of
the first Caribbean food

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.440
and drink beverage places.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.980
So they used to have a house on Moslanes
in Manchester, called Mother

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:13.860
Bees Establishment.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.800
285 Moslanes East Street, Mother Bees
Establishment is also a

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.640
poem in the book

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.960
where she used to sell food to Jamaican

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.700
food, West Indian food, whatever you want
to call it,

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.700
to communities coming in and they also had
a

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.320
bit of an illegal drinking house

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.420
at weekends in the cellar that was called
a Shabeen and that was

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:40.720
about

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.400
people not being able to go into the city
centre you know it was

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:44.780
quite a

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.340
hostile in the 60s and early 70s when
black people wanted to go out

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.500
into into

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.620
town and dance there would be a lot of
opposition and so my parents

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.120
were about

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:00.420
providing people with the means to meet
each other, fall in love,

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.480
dream and have a

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.240
good time until the early hours of the
morning. The work ethic was

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:06.940
always about

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:11.140
making things happen because you could and
not allowing other people

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:11.720
to stand in

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.660
your way and to sidestep the people who
want to stand in your way

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:16.800
and to take you

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.060
down.
